# My-First-Rspository
Class Work
Go to github.com and sign in to your  account.
Start creating a new repository
Click the + icon in the top-right corner, then select New repository.
Configure the repository
Choose your personal account as the Owner.
Enter a name in the Repository name box.
Optional: add a short description.
Under visibility, select Private.
Under “Initialize this repository,” check Add a README file.
Create the repository
Click the green Create repository button at the bottom of the page.
Check the result
On the new repository page, confirm that:
A Private label appears next to the repository name.
The file list contains README.md.
The README content is displayed automatically below the file list.
